# === Agent / IDE / CLI session scratch directories ===========================
#
# Every modern coding-agent CLI and AI-aware IDE drops per-session
# sandboxes, worktrees, indexes, or cache somewhere. When those land
# in the repo root they get visually noisy on GitHub *and* risk
# leaking scratch artifacts into commits via `git add -A`.
#
# Historical incident: PR #20 (squash-merged 2026-05-28) brought two
# stray files under `.claire/worktrees/...` and `.clone/worktrees/...`
# into the index because neither pattern was ignored at the time. See
# the post-mortem note in commit message of the patch that added these
# expanded entries.
#
# Patterns below are the union of dot-dirs that have shown up across
# coding agents (Cursor, Cursor's "Claire", clone-of variants, Claude
# Code, Cline, Codex, Continue, Aider, Windsurf, Qoder, …) plus the
# CLIs in this repo's own ecosystem (clide, tide, deeptide). Anything
# matching is per-developer or per-session and should never be
# committed.
.clide/
.clideignore
.tide/
.claude/
.claire/
.clone/
.cursor-server/
.cline/
.codex/
.continue/
.aider*/
.windsurf/
.qoder/
# Defensive wildcards for variants we haven't enumerated yet. Many
# agent CLIs name their per-session sandbox `agent-<hash>/`; we
# match those only when they live under a `worktrees/` parent (the
# observed historical shape) so a real project directory called
# e.g. `agent-runtime/` is not accidentally swallowed.
**/worktrees/agent-*/
# Note on intentional non-ignores: `.deeptide/` and `.cursor/` are
# NOT in this list. They hold team-shared, intentionally-committed
# content (`.deeptide/settings.json` for project config, `.cursor/
# rules/*.mdc` for shared AI rules). Their per-developer overrides
# (`.deeptide/settings.local.json`) live next to the shared file and
# are handled by the more specific entries below.
.deeptide/settings.local.json
# =============================================================================
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# `deeptide-rs` npm package: the postinstall downloader drops the
# platform-specific Rust binary into npm/deeptide-rs/binary/ on
# `npm install`. Tracking it would balloon the repo and is the
# release pipeline's responsibility, not git's.
npm/deeptide-rs/binary/

# Native runtime build outputs. Source under native/ is intentionally tracked.
native/ds4/ds4
native/ds4/ds4-server
native/ds4/ds4_test
native/ds4/*.o
native/ds4/gguf/
native/ds4/*.gguf
native/dsgo/.build/
native/dsgo/models/
native/dsgo/*.log
native/dsgo/anthropic_gateway/
